# Data Loading | TanStack Router Solid Docs
created: undefined, last updated: 2026-03-29, [Read more](https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/solid/guide/data-loading)

Every time a URL/history update is detected, the router executes the following sequence:
- Route Matching (Top-Down) - route.params.parse
- route.validateSearch
- Route Pre-Loading (Serial) - route.beforeLoad
- route.onError - route.errorComponent / parentRoute.errorComponent / router.defaultErrorComponent
...
### Accessing Search Params via routeOptions.loaderDeps
```
// /routes/posts.tsx
export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({
// Use zod to validate and parse the search params
validateSearch: z.object({
offset: z.number().int().nonnegative().catch(0),
}),
// Pass the offset to your loader deps via the loaderDeps function
loaderDeps: ({ search: { offset } }) => ({ offset }),
// Use the offset from context in the loader function
loader: async ({ deps: { offset } }) =>
fetchPosts({
offset,
}),
})
```

